{
  "info": {
    "name": "Plataforma MOOC — Entrega 1",
    "description": "Colección de la demostración de aceptación. Una carpeta por segmento de la sección 10.2 del enunciado.\n\n**Uso:** importar junto con `mooc.postman_environment.json`, levantar el stack con `make up` y ejecutar las carpetas en orden con el Collection Runner.\n\nLas carpetas vacías son segmentos cuyo módulo todavía no existe: el hueco se deja visible a propósito, para que el avance se mida contra la demostración y no contra el número de endpoints.\n\nEstado: SEG-1 parcial (falta `admin`); SEG-2 a SEG-8 pendientes; SEG-9 parcial.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "SEG-1 · Identidad y administración",
      "description": "Registro de estudiante, verificación de correo, sesiones revocables y rechazo de operaciones no autorizadas.\n\nCriterio: identidad, autorización y seguridad (CE-02).\nRequisitos: RF-01, RF-02, CA-06.\n\nEl token de verificación se lee de Mailpit: ejecuta «Leer token del correo» después de registrar.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Salud — readyz",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/readyz",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "readyz"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Comprueba PostgreSQL, Redis y el almacén de objetos (ADR-0009)."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('postgres ok', () => pm.expect(d.postgres).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('redis ok', () => pm.expect(d.redis).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('objectstore ok', () => pm.expect(d.objectstore).to.eql('ok'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Registro inválido — lista exhaustiva de errores",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "La API devuelve TODOS los incumplimientos en un solo 422, no el primero. Es la mecánica que CA-01 exige para la publicación de un curso.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"no-es-un-correo\",\n  \"password\": \"corta\",\n  \"full_name\": \"\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('application/problem+json (RFC 9457)', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/problem+json'));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('trae trace_id para correlacionar', () => pm.expect(d.trace_id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('acumula los tres errores', () => pm.expect(d.errors).to.have.lengthOf(3));",
                  "pm.test('cada error trae código y campo', () =>",
                  "  d.errors.forEach(e => { pm.expect(e.code).to.be.a('string'); pm.expect(e.field).to.be.a('string'); }));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Registro de estudiante",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Responde 202: la API no espera al worker que envía el correo (CA-02).\nEl correo electrónico se genera con marca de tiempo para poder repetir la demo.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{nuevo_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{demo_password}}\",\n  \"full_name\": \"Estudiante de Demostración\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Correo único por ejecución, para que la demo sea repetible.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('nuevo_email', `estudiante+${Date.now()}@mooc.local`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('202 Accepted — no bloquea esperando al worker', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('queda pendiente de verificación', () => pm.expect(d.status).to.eql('pending_verification'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', d.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Leer token del correo (Mailpit)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/search?query=to:{{nuevo_email}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "search?query=to:{{nuevo_email}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Lee el buzón de Mailpit. Sustituye la URL base por {{mailpit_url}} en la pestaña de la petición si Postman no la resuelve.\n\nEvidencia de que el worker consumió el trabajo de la cola."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('el worker entregó el correo', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.expect(d.messages, 'no llegó ningún correo').to.have.length.above(0);",
                  "const id = d.messages[0].ID;",
                  "pm.sendRequest(`${pm.collectionVariables.get('mailpit_url')}/api/v1/message/${id}`, (err, res) => {",
                  "  const texto = res.json().Text;",
                  "  const m = texto.match(/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{40,}\\r?$/m);",
                  "  pm.test('el correo trae el token de verificación', () => pm.expect(m).to.not.be.null);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('verify_token', m[1] || m[0].trim());",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verificar el correo",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/verify-email",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "verify-email"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{verify_token}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('verificado', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().verified).to.be.true);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Reutilizar el token — debe fallar",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/verify-email",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "verify-email"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Un token de un solo uso no se puede consumir dos veces.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{verify_token}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 al reutilizarlo', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login con contraseña incorrecta",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Mismo 401 para usuario inexistente, contraseña incorrecta y cuenta sin verificar: no se revela qué correos existen.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{nuevo_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"incorrecta\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{nuevo_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{demo_password}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('devuelve token de sesión', () => pm.expect(d.token).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.test('el registro público solo crea estudiantes (RF-01)', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(d.user.role).to.eql('student'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('session_token', d.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /me",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{session_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('correo verificado', () => pm.expect(d.email_verified_at).to.not.be.null);",
                  "pm.test('nunca expone el hash de la contraseña', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('password'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /me sin sesión",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Control de acceso: cada endpoint respeta rol y sesión (CA-06)."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
